r":1.5,"landingRailLf":8,"skirtingAccessDoor":1000,"skirtingPartialShare":0.5,"privacyWallPerLf":300,"stairOpeningLf":4,"expansionIntegration":0.08,"redeckFramingContingency":0.1},"ranges":{"standard":[0.9,1.1],"uncertain":[0.85,1.18],"review":[0.8,1.25]},"serviceArea":{"primaryZipPrefixes":["193","194","195"],"edgeZipPrefixes":["175","176","180","181","189","190","191"]},"copy":{"steps":["Project","Size","Site","Material","Railings","Stairs","Existing deck","Finishing","Your estimate"],"intro":"What should you realistically budget for your deck? Nine short steps, about 3 minutes. \"Not sure\" is always fine, and rough measurements are OK. At the end we ask where to reach you, then show your price range.","serviceArea":{"primary":"Your project appears to fall within our typical service and project range.","edge":"Your project is near the edge of our service area. Availability may depend on project size and location.","outside":"Thanks! Your ZIP code may be outside the area we currently serve, but send your details and we''ll let you know."},"disclaimers":{"primary":"This online estimate is intended for early budgeting and planning only. It is not a formal proposal, contract, or guarantee of price. Final pricing depends on site measurements, structural requirements, access, township and permit requirements, material selections, existing conditions, and the final approved design.","redeck":"Redeck pricing assumes the existing footings, ledger, posts, beams, joists, stairs, and related framing are structurally sound, properly sized, code-compliant, and suitable for reuse. Repairs or upgrades identified after removal of the existing decking are not included unless specifically stated.","permit":"Permit fees and municipal requirements vary by township. The estimate includes a standard planning allowance unless otherwise noted. Engineering, zoning relief, variances, surveys, or unusual municipal requirements may require additional pricing.","material":"Material pricing can vary by manufacturer, product line, color, availability, and market conditions. Final material selections are confirmed before a formal proposal is issued.","homeownerDemo":"If you remove the existing deck yourself, the site must be fully cleared, safe, and ready before construction begins.","lighting":"Electrical upgrades, new circuits, transformer locations, outlets, and related house wiring may require separate pricing.","neighbors":"Neighboring projects may qualify for shared-mobilization savings. Final eligibility is confirmed during the proposal process.","townhouseHoa":"Townhouses and HOA properties often have shared walls, setback rules, or approval steps that change the price. Treat this range as a starting point and call us for pricing on your property."},"included":["Standard footings and framing","Your selected decking material and standard fastening","One picture-frame border on composite decks","Selected railings, stairs, and landings","Standard fascia","Demolition and disposal, if selected","Standard permit allowance","General jobsite cleanup"],"priceFactors":["Existing framing condition","Footing and soil requirements","Township and HOA requirements","Final railing measurements and stair layout","Property access","Material colors and product lines","Structural engineering","Utility conflicts or hidden damage","Final design selections"]}}', 1);
